msgstr ""
"und fügen Sie es in das Element „ :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new` “ ein::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:323
msgid ".tp_new = Custom_new,"
msgstr ".tp_new = Custom_new,"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:325
msgid ""
"The ``tp_new`` handler is responsible for creating (as opposed to "
"initializing) objects of the type.  It is exposed in Python as the :meth:"
"`~object.__new__` method. It is not required to define a ``tp_new`` member, "
"and indeed many extension types will simply reuse :c:func:"
"`PyType_GenericNew` as done in the first version of the :class:`!Custom` "
"type above.  In this case, we use the ``tp_new`` handler to initialize the "
"``first`` and ``last`` attributes to non-``NULL`` default values."
msgstr ""
"Der Handler „ ``tp_new`` “ ist für die Erstellung (im Gegensatz zur "
"Initialisierung) von Objekten dieses Typs zuständig. Er wird in Python als "
"Methode „ :meth:`~object.__new__` “ bereitgestellt. Es ist nicht "
"erforderlich, ein „ ``tp_new`` “-Mitglied zu definieren, und tatsächlich "
"verwenden viele Erweiterungstypen einfach „ :c:func:`PyType_GenericNew` “ "
"wieder, wie dies in der ersten Version des oben genannten Typs „ :class:`!"
"Custom` “ der Fall ist.  In diesem Fall verwenden wir den Handler "
"„ ``tp_new`` “, um die Attribute „ ``first`` “ und „ ``last`` “ auf "
"Standardwerte zu initialisieren, die nicht „``NULL`` “ sind."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:333
msgid ""
"``tp_new`` is passed the type being instantiated (not necessarily "
"``CustomType``, if a subclass is instantiated) and any arguments passed when "
"the type was called, and is expected to return the instance created.  "
"``tp_new`` handlers always accept positional and keyword arguments, but they "
"often ignore the arguments, leaving the argument handling to initializer (a."
"k.a. ``tp_init`` in C or ``__init__`` in Python) methods."
msgstr ""
"``tp_new`` Erhält den zu instanziierenden Typ (nicht unbedingt ` "
"``CustomType```, wenn eine Unterklasse instanziiert wird) sowie alle "
"Argumente, die beim Aufruf des Typs übergeben wurden, und soll die erstellte "
"Instanz zurückgeben. ``tp_new`` Handler akzeptieren immer Positions- und "
"Schlüsselwortargumente, ignorieren diese jedoch häufig und überlassen die "
"Argumentverarbeitung den Initialisierungsmethoden (auch bekannt als "
"„ ``tp_init`` “ in C oder „ ``__init__`` “ in Python)."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:341
msgid ""
"``tp_new`` shouldn't call ``tp_init`` explicitly, as the interpreter will do "
"it itself."
msgstr ""
"``tp_new`` Man sollte ` ``tp_init`` ` nicht explizit aufrufen, da der "
"Interpreter dies selbst übernimmt."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:344
msgid ""
"The ``tp_new`` implementation calls the :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_alloc` "
"slot to allocate memory::"
msgstr ""
"Die Implementierung von ` ``tp_new`` ` ruft den Slot ` :c:member:"
"`~PyTypeObject.tp_alloc` ` auf, um Speicher zuzuweisen::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:347
msgid "self = (CustomObject *) type->tp_alloc(type, 0);"
msgstr "self = (CustomObject *) type->tp_alloc(type, 0);"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:349
msgid ""
"Since memory allocation may fail, we must check the :c:member:`~PyTypeObject."
"tp_alloc` result against ``NULL`` before proceeding."
msgstr ""
"Da die Speicherzuweisung fehlschlagen kann, müssen wir das Ergebnis von ` :c:"
"member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_alloc` ` mit ` ``NULL`` ` vergleichen, bevor wir "
"fortfahren."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:353
msgid ""
"We didn't fill the :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_alloc` slot ourselves. "
"Rather :c:func:`PyType_Ready` fills it for us by inheriting it from our base "
"class, which is :class:`object` by default.  Most types use the default "
"allocation strategy."
msgstr ""
"Wir haben das ` :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_alloc` `-Interface nicht selbst "
"implementiert. Stattdessen übernimmt ` :c:func:`PyType_Ready` ` dies für "
"uns, indem es es von unserer Basisklasse erbt, die standardmäßig ` :class:"
"`object` ` ist. Die meisten Typen verwenden die Standard-Zuweisungsstrategie."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:359
msgid ""
"If you are creating a co-operative :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new` (one "
"that calls a base type's :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new` or :meth:`~object."
"__new__`), you must *not* try to determine what method to call using method "
"resolution order at runtime.  Always statically determine what type you are "
"going to call, and call its :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new` directly, or "
"via ``type->tp_base->tp_new``.  If you do not do this, Python subclasses of "
"your type that also inherit from other Python-defined classes may not work "
"correctly. (Specifically, you may not be able to create instances of such "
"subclasses without getting a :exc:`TypeError`.)"
msgstr ""
"Wenn Sie eine kooperative „ :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new` “ erstellen "
"(d. h. eine, die „ :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new` “ oder „ :meth:`~object."
"__new__` “ eines Basistyps aufruft), dürfen Sie *nicht* versuchen, zur "
"Laufzeit anhand der Methodenauflösungsreihenfolge zu ermitteln, welche "
"Methode aufgerufen werden soll.  Legen Sie immer statisch fest, welchen Typ "
"Sie aufrufen möchten, und rufen Sie dessen ` :c:member:`~PyTypeObject."
"tp_new` ` direkt oder über ` ``type->tp_base->tp_new``` auf.  Wenn Sie dies "
"nicht tun, funktionieren Python-Unterklassen Ihres Typs, die auch von "
"anderen in Python definierten Klassen erben, möglicherweise nicht korrekt. "
"(Insbesondere können Sie möglicherweise keine Instanzen solcher Unterklassen "
"erstellen, ohne eine ` :exc:`TypeError`` zu erhalten.)"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:369
msgid ""
"We also define an initialization function which accepts arguments to provide "
"initial values for our instance::"
msgstr ""
"Außerdem definieren wir eine Initialisierungsfunktion, die Argumente "
"entgegennimmt, um Anfangswerte für unsere Instanz bereitzustellen::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:372
msgid ""
"static int\n"
"Custom_init(PyObject *op, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwds)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    static char *kwlist[] = {\"first\", \"last\", \"number\", NULL};\n"
"    PyObject *first = NULL, *last = NULL, *tmp;\n"
"\n"
"    if (!PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords(args, kwds, \"|OOi\", kwlist,\n"
"                                     &first, &last,\n"
"                                     &self->number))\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"\n"
"    if (first) {\n"
"        tmp = self->first;\n"
"        Py_INCREF(first);\n"
"        self->first = first;\n"
"        Py_XDECREF(tmp);\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (last) {\n"
"        tmp = self->last;\n"
"        Py_INCREF(last);\n"
"        self->last = last;\n"
"        Py_XDECREF(tmp);\n"
"    }\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"static int\n"
"Custom_init(PyObject *op, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwds)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    static char *kwlist[] = {\"first\", \"last\", \"number\", NULL};\n"
"    PyObject *first = NULL, *last = NULL, *tmp;\n"
"\n"
"    if (!PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords(args, kwds, \"|OOi\", kwlist,\n"
"                                     &first, &last,\n"
"                                     &self->number))\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"\n"
"    if (first) {\n"
"        tmp = self->first;\n"
"        Py_INCREF(first);\n"
"        self->first = first;\n"
"        Py_XDECREF(tmp);\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (last) {\n"
"        tmp = self->last;\n"
"        Py_INCREF(last);\n"
"        self->last = last;\n"
"        Py_XDECREF(tmp);\n"
"    }\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:399
msgid "by filling the :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_init` slot. ::"
msgstr ""
"indem die Stelle als „ :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_init` “ besetzt wird. ::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:401
msgid ".tp_init = Custom_init,"
msgstr ".tp_init = Custom_init,"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:403
msgid ""
"The :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_init` slot is exposed in Python as the :meth:"
"`~object.__init__` method.  It is used to initialize an object after it's "
"created.  Initializers always accept positional and keyword arguments, and "
"they should return either ``0`` on success or ``-1`` on error."
msgstr ""
"Der Slot „ :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_init` “ wird in Python als Methode „ :"
"meth:`~object.__init__` “ bereitgestellt. Er dient dazu, ein Objekt nach "
"seiner Erstellung zu initialisieren. Initialisierer akzeptieren immer "
"Positions- und Schlüsselwortargumente und sollten bei Erfolg „ ``0`` “ oder "
"bei einem Fehler „ ``-1`` “ zurückgeben."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:408
msgid ""
"Unlike the ``tp_new`` handler, there is no guarantee that ``tp_init`` is "
"called at all (for example, the :mod:`pickle` module by default doesn't "
"call :meth:`~object.__init__` on unpickled instances).  It can also be "
"called multiple times.  Anyone can call the :meth:`!__init__` method on our "
"objects.  For this reason, we have to be extra careful when assigning the "
"new attribute values.  We might be tempted, for example to assign the "
"``first`` member like this::"
msgstr ""
"Im Gegensatz zum Handler „ ``tp_new`` “ gibt es keine Garantie dafür, dass "
"„ ``tp_init`` “ überhaupt aufgerufen wird (beispielsweise ruft das Modul „ :"
"mod:`pickle` “ standardmäßig „ :meth:`~object.__init__` “ bei nicht-pickled "
"Instanzen nicht auf). Es kann auch mehrfach aufgerufen werden. Jeder kann "
"die Methode „ :meth:`!__init__` “ für unsere Objekte aufrufen.  Aus diesem "
"Grund müssen wir bei der Zuweisung der neuen Attributwerte besonders "
"vorsichtig sein. Wir könnten beispielsweise versucht sein, das Element ` "
"``first`` ` wie folgt zuzuweisen::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:416
msgid ""
"if (first) {\n"
"    Py_XDECREF(self->first);\n"
"    Py_INCREF(first);\n"
"    self->first = first;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"if (first) {\n"
"    Py_XDECREF(self->first);\n"
"    Py_INCREF(first);\n"
"    self->first = first;\n"
"}"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:422
msgid ""
"But this would be risky.  Our type doesn't restrict the type of the "
"``first`` member, so it could be any kind of object.  It could have a "
"destructor that causes code to be executed that tries to access the "
"``first`` member; or that destructor could detach the :term:`thread state "
"<attached thread state>` and let arbitrary code run in other threads that "
"accesses and modifies our object."
msgstr ""
"Das wäre jedoch riskant.  Unser Typ schränkt den Typ des Mitglieds ` "
"``first`` ` nicht ein, sodass es sich um ein beliebiges Objekt handeln "
"könnte.  Es könnte einen Destruktor haben, der die Ausführung von Code "
"auslöst, der versucht, auf das Mitglied ` ``first`` ` zuzugreifen; oder "
"dieser Destruktor könnte den :term:`Thread-Status <attached thread state>` "
"trennen und beliebigen Code in anderen Threads ausführen lassen, der auf "
"unser Objekt zugreift und es verändert."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:429
msgid ""
"To be paranoid and protect ourselves against this possibility, we almost "
"always reassign members before decrementing their reference counts.  When "
"don't we have to do this?"
msgstr ""
"Um auf Nummer sicher zu gehen und uns vor dieser Möglichkeit zu schützen, "
"weisen wir Elemente fast immer neu zu, bevor wir ihre Referenzzähler "
"verringern. Wann müssen wir das nicht tun?"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:433
msgid "when we absolutely know that the reference count is greater than 1;"
msgstr ""
"wenn wir mit absoluter Sicherheit wissen, dass die Referenzanzahl größer als "
"1 ist;"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:435
msgid ""
"when we know that deallocation of the object [#]_ will neither detach the :"
"term:`thread state <attached thread state>` nor cause any calls back into "
"our type's code;"
msgstr ""
"wenn wir wissen, dass die Freigabe des Objekts [#]_ weder den :term:`Thread-"
"Zustand <attached thread state>` trennt noch Rückrufe in den Code unseres "
"Typs auslöst;"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:438
msgid ""
"when decrementing a reference count in a :c:member:`~PyTypeObject."
"tp_dealloc` handler on a type which doesn't support cyclic garbage "
"collection [#]_."
msgstr ""
"beim Herabsetzen einer Referenzanzahl in einem ` :c:member:`~PyTypeObject."
"tp_dealloc` `-Handler für einen Typ, der keine zyklische Garbage Collection "
"unterstützt [#]_."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:441
msgid ""
"We want to expose our instance variables as attributes. There are a number "
"of ways to do that. The simplest way is to define member definitions::"
msgstr ""
"Wir möchten unsere Instanzvariablen als Attribute verfügbar machen. Dafür "
"gibt es verschiedene Möglichkeiten. Am einfachsten ist es, Member-"
"Definitionen zu definieren::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:444
msgid ""
"static PyMemberDef Custom_members[] = {\n"
"    {\"first\", Py_T_OBJECT_EX, offsetof(CustomObject, first), 0,\n"
"     \"first name\"},\n"
"    {\"last\", Py_T_OBJECT_EX, offsetof(CustomObject, last), 0,\n"
"     \"last name\"},\n"
"    {\"number\", Py_T_INT, offsetof(CustomObject, number), 0,\n"
"     \"custom number\"},\n"
"    {NULL}  /* Sentinel */\n"
"};"
msgstr ""
"static PyMemberDef Custom_members[] = {\n"
"    {\"first\", Py_T_OBJECT_EX, offsetof(CustomObject, first), 0,\n"
"     \"Vorname\"},\n"
"    {\"last\", Py_T_OBJECT_EX, offsetof(CustomObject, last), 0,\n"
"     „Nachname“},\n"
"    {\"number\", Py_T_INT, offsetof(CustomObject, number), 0,\n"
"     „benutzerdefinierte Nummer“},\n"
"    {NULL}  /* Sentinel */\n"
"};"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:454
msgid ""
"and put the definitions in the :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_members` slot::"
msgstr ""
"und füge die Definitionen in den Bereich „ :c:member:`~PyTypeObject."
"tp_members` “ ein::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:456
msgid ".tp_members = Custom_members,"
msgstr ".tp_members = Custom_members,"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:458
msgid ""
"Each member definition has a member name, type, offset, access flags and "
"documentation string.  See the :ref:`Generic-Attribute-Management` section "
"below for details."
msgstr ""
"Jede Member-Definition verfügt über einen Member-Namen, einen Typ, einen "
"Offset, Zugriffsflags und eine Dokumentationszeichenfolge. Weitere "
"Informationen finden Sie im Abschnitt „ :ref:`Generic-Attribute-Management` "
"“ weiter unten."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:462
msgid ""
"A disadvantage of this approach is that it doesn't provide a way to restrict "
"the types of objects that can be assigned to the Python attributes.  We "
"expect the first and last names to be strings, but any Python objects can be "
"assigned. Further, the attributes can be deleted, setting the C pointers to "
"``NULL``.  Even though we can make sure the members are initialized to non-"
"``NULL`` values, the members can be set to ``NULL`` if the attributes are "
"deleted."
msgstr ""
"Ein Nachteil dieses Ansatzes besteht darin, dass er keine Möglichkeit "
"bietet, die Typen der Objekte einzuschränken, die den Python-Attributen "
"zugewiesen werden können. Wir gehen davon aus, dass Vor- und Nachname "
"Zeichenketten sind, es können jedoch beliebige Python-Objekte zugewiesen "
"werden. Außerdem können die Attribute gelöscht werden, wodurch die C-Zeiger "
"auf ` ``NULL``` gesetzt werden.  Auch wenn wir sicherstellen können, dass "
"die Elemente auf Werte initialisiert werden, die nicht ```NULL`` ` sind, "
"können die Elemente auf ` ``NULL`` ` gesetzt werden, wenn die Attribute "
"gelöscht werden."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:469
msgid ""
"We define a single method, :meth:`!Custom.name`, that outputs the objects "
"name as the concatenation of the first and last names. ::"
msgstr ""
"Wir definieren eine einzige Methode, „ :meth:`!Custom.name` “, die den Namen "
"des Objekts als Verkettung von Vor- und Nachnamen ausgibt. ::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:472
msgid ""
"static PyObject *\n"
"Custom_name(PyObject *op, PyObject *Py_UNUSED(dummy))\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    if (self->first == NULL) {\n"
"        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_AttributeError, \"first\");\n"
"        return NULL;\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (self->last == NULL) {\n"
"        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_AttributeError, \"last\");\n"
"        return NULL;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return PyUnicode_FromFormat(\"%S %S\", self->first, self->last);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"static PyObject *\n"
"Custom_name(PyObject *op, PyObject *Py_UNUSED(dummy))\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    if (self->first == NULL) {\n"
"        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_AttributeError, \"first\");\n"
"        return NULL;\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (self->last == NULL) {\n"
"        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_AttributeError, \"last\");\n"
"        return NULL;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return PyUnicode_FromFormat(\"%S %S\", self->first, self->last);\n"
"}"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:487
msgid ""
"The method is implemented as a C function that takes a :class:`!Custom` (or :"
"class:`!Custom` subclass) instance as the first argument.  Methods always "
"take an instance as the first argument. Methods often take positional and "
"keyword arguments as well, but in this case we don't take any and don't need "
"to accept a positional argument tuple or keyword argument dictionary. This "
"method is equivalent to the Python method:"
msgstr ""
"Die Methode ist als C-Funktion implementiert, die eine Instanz von ` :class:"
"`!Custom` ` (oder einer Unterklasse von ` :class:`!Custom` `) als erstes "
"Argument entgegennimmt.  Methoden nehmen immer eine Instanz als erstes "
"Argument entgegen. Oft nehmen Methoden auch Positions- und "
"Schlüsselwortargumente entgegen, doch in diesem Fall nehmen wir keine "
"entgegen und müssen weder ein Tupel mit Positionsargumenten noch ein "
"Wörterbuch mit Schlüsselwortargumenten akzeptieren. Diese Methode entspricht "
"der Python-Methode:"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:494
msgid ""
"def name(self):\n"
"    return \"%s %s\" % (self.first, self.last)"
msgstr ""
"def name(self):\n"
"    return \"%s %s \" % (self.first, self.last)"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:499
msgid ""
"Note that we have to check for the possibility that our :attr:`!first` and :"
"attr:`!last` members are ``NULL``.  This is because they can be deleted, in "
"which case they are set to ``NULL``.  It would be better to prevent deletion "
"of these attributes and to restrict the attribute values to be strings.  "
"We'll see how to do that in the next section."
msgstr ""
"Beachten Sie, dass wir die Möglichkeit berücksichtigen müssen, dass unsere "
"Elemente „ :attr:`!first` “ und „ :attr:`!last` “ den Wert „ ``NULL`` “ "
"annehmen können. Der Grund dafür ist, dass sie gelöscht werden können; in "
"diesem Fall werden sie auf „ ``NULL`` “ gesetzt. Es wäre besser, das Löschen "
"dieser Attribute zu verhindern und die Attributwerte auf Zeichenketten zu "
"beschränken. Wie das geht, sehen wir im nächsten Abschnitt."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:505
msgid ""
"Now that we've defined the method, we need to create an array of method "
"definitions::"
msgstr ""
"Nachdem wir nun die Methode definiert haben, müssen wir ein Array mit "
"Methodendefinitionen erstellen::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:508
msgid ""
"static PyMethodDef Custom_methods[] = {\n"
"    {\"name\", Custom_name, METH_NOARGS,\n"
"     \"Return the name, combining the first and last name\"\n"
"    },\n"
"    {NULL}  /* Sentinel */\n"
"};"
msgstr ""
"static PyMethodDef Custom_methods[] = {\n"
"    {\"name\", Custom_name, METH_NOARGS,\n"
"     \"Gibt den Namen zurück, der aus Vor- und Nachnamen zusammengesetzt "
"ist\"\n"
"    },\n"
"    {NULL}  /* Sentinel */\n"
"};"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:515
msgid ""
"(note that we used the :c:macro:`METH_NOARGS` flag to indicate that the "
"method is expecting no arguments other than *self*)"
msgstr ""
"(Beachten Sie, dass wir das Flag „ :c:macro:`METH_NOARGS` “ verwendet haben, "
"um anzugeben, dass die Methode außer *self* keine weiteren Argumente "
"erwartet.)"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:518
msgid "and assign it to the :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_methods` slot::"
msgstr ""
"und weisen Sie es dem Slot „ :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_methods` “ zu::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:520
msgid ".tp_methods = Custom_methods,"
msgstr ".tp_methods = Custom_methods,"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:522
msgid ""
"Finally, we'll make our type usable as a base class for subclassing.  We've "
"written our methods carefully so far so that they don't make any assumptions "
"about the type of the object being created or used, so all we need to do is "
"to add the :c:macro:`Py_TPFLAGS_BASETYPE` to our class flag definition::"
msgstr ""
"Abschließend machen wir unseren Typ als Basisklasse für Unterklassen "
"nutzbar. Da wir unsere Methoden bisher sorgfältig so geschrieben haben, dass "
"sie keine Annahmen über den Typ des erstellten oder verwendeten Objekts "
"treffen, müssen wir lediglich die Anweisung „ :c:macro:`Py_TPFLAGS_BASETYPE` "
"“ zu unserer Klassendefinition hinzufügen::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:527
msgid ".tp_flags = Py_TPFLAGS_DEFAULT | Py_TPFLAGS_BASETYPE,"
msgstr ".tp_flags = Py_TPFLAGS_DEFAULT | Py_TPFLAGS_BASETYPE,"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:529
msgid ""
"We rename :c:func:`!PyInit_custom` to :c:func:`!PyInit_custom2`, update the "
"module name in the :c:type:`PyModuleDef` struct, and update the full class "
"name in the :c:type:`PyTypeObject` struct."
msgstr ""
"Wir benennen „ :c:func:`!PyInit_custom` “ in „ :c:func:`!PyInit_custom2` “ "
"um, aktualisieren den Modulnamen in der Struktur „ :c:type:`PyModuleDef` “ "
"und den vollständigen Klassennamen in der Struktur „ :c:type:`PyTypeObject` "
"“."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:533
msgid "Finally, we update our :file:`setup.py` file to include the new module,"
msgstr ""
"Abschließend aktualisieren wir unsere Datei „ :file:`setup.py` “, um das "
"neue Modul einzubinden,"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:535
msgid ""
"from setuptools import Extension, setup\n"
"setup(ext_modules=[\n"
"    Extension(\"custom\", [\"custom.c\"]),\n"
"    Extension(\"custom2\", [\"custom2.c\"]),\n"
"])"
msgstr ""
"from setuptools import Extension, setup\n"
"setup(ext_modules=[\n"
"    Extension(\"custom\", [\"custom.c\"]),\n"
"    Extension(\"custom2\", [\"custom2.c\"]),\n"
"])"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:543
msgid "and then we re-install so that we can ``import custom2``:"
msgstr ""
"und dann führen wir die Neuinstallation durch, damit wir ``import custom2`` "
"nutzen können:"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:550
msgid "Providing finer control over data attributes"
msgstr "Eine präzisere Steuerung der Datenattribute ermöglichen"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:552
msgid ""
"In this section, we'll provide finer control over how the :attr:`!first` "
"and :attr:`!last` attributes are set in the :class:`!Custom` example. In the "
"previous version of our module, the instance variables :attr:`!first` and :"
"attr:`!last` could be set to non-string values or even deleted. We want to "
"make sure that these attributes always contain strings."
msgstr ""
"In diesem Abschnitt werden wir eine genauere Kontrolle darüber ermöglichen, "
"wie die Attribute „ :attr:`!first` “ und „ :attr:`!last` “ im Beispiel „ :"
"class:`!Custom` “ gesetzt werden. In der vorherigen Version unseres Moduls "
"konnten die Instanzvariablen „ :attr:`!first` “ und „ :attr:`!last` “ auf "
"Nicht-Zeichenfolgenwerte gesetzt oder sogar gelöscht werden. Wir möchten "
"sicherstellen, dass diese Attribute immer Zeichenfolgen enthalten."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:558
msgid ""
"#define PY_SSIZE_T_CLEAN\n"
"#include <Python.h>\n"
"#include <stddef.h> /* for offsetof() */\n"
"\n"
"typedef struct {\n"
"    PyObject_HEAD\n"
"    PyObject *first; /* first name */\n"
"    PyObject *last;  /* last name */\n"
"    int number;\n"
"} CustomObject;\n"
"\n"
"static void\n"
"Custom_dealloc(PyObject *op)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    Py_XDECREF(self->first);\n"
"    Py_XDECREF(self->last);\n"
"    Py_TYPE(self)->tp_free(self);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyObject *\n"
"Custom_new(PyTypeObject *type, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwds)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self;\n"
"    self = (CustomObject *) type->tp_alloc(type, 0);\n"
"    if (self != NULL) {\n"
"        self->first = Py_GetConstant(Py_CONSTANT_EMPTY_STR);\n"
"        if (self->first == NULL) {\n"
"            Py_DECREF(self);\n"
"            return NULL;\n"
"        }\n"
"        self->last = Py_GetConstant(Py_CONSTANT_EMPTY_STR);\n"
"        if (self->last == NULL) {\n"
"            Py_DECREF(self);\n"
"            return NULL;\n"
"        }\n"
"        self->number = 0;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return (PyObject *) self;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static int\n"
"Custom_init(PyObject *op, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwds)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    static char *kwlist[] = {\"first\", \"last\", \"number\", NULL};\n"
"    PyObject *first = NULL, *last = NULL;\n"
"\n"
"    if (!PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords(args, kwds, \"|UUi\", kwlist,\n"
"                                     &first, &last,\n"
"                                     &self->number))\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"\n"
"    if (first) {\n"
"        Py_SETREF(self->first, Py_NewRef(first));\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (last) {\n"
"        Py_SETREF(self->last, Py_NewRef(last));\n"
"    }\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyMemberDef Custom_members[] = {\n"
"    {\"number\", Py_T_INT, offsetof(CustomObject, number), 0,\n"
"     \"custom number\"},\n"
"    {NULL}  /* Sentinel */\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static PyObject *\n"
"Custom_getfirst(PyObject *op, void *closure)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    return Py_NewRef(self->first);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static int\n"
"Custom_setfirst(PyObject *op, PyObject *value, void *closure)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    if (value == NULL) {\n"
"        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_TypeError, \"Cannot delete the first "
"attribute\");\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (!PyUnicode_Check(value)) {\n"
"        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_TypeError,\n"
"                        \"The first attribute value must be a string\");\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    Py_SETREF(self->first, Py_NewRef(value));\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyObject *\n"
"Custom_getlast(PyObject *op, void *closure)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    return Py_NewRef(self->last);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static int\n"
"Custom_setlast(PyObject *op, PyObject *value, void *closure)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    if (value == NULL) {\n"
"        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_TypeError, \"Cannot delete the last "
"attribute\");\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (!PyUnicode_Check(value)) {\n"
"        PyErr_SetString(PyExc_TypeError,\n"
"                        \"The last attribute value must be a string\");\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    Py_SETREF(self->last, Py_NewRef(value));\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyGetSetDef Custom_getsetters[] = {\n"
"    {\"first\", Custom_getfirst, Custom_setfirst,\n"
"     \"first name\", NULL},\n"
"    {\"last\", Custom_getlast, Custom_setlast,\n"
"     \"last name\", NULL},\n"
"    {NULL}  /* Sentinel */\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static PyObject *\n"
"Custom_name(PyObject *op, PyObject *Py_UNUSED(dummy))\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    return PyUnicode_FromFormat(\"%S %S\", self->first, self->last);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyMethodDef Custom_methods[] = {\n"
"    {\"name\", Custom_name, METH_NOARGS,\n"
"     \"Return the name, combining the first and last name\"\n"
"    },\n"
"    {NULL}  /* Sentinel */\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static PyTypeObject CustomType = {\n"
"    .ob_base = PyVarObject_HEAD_INIT(NULL, 0)\n"
"    .tp_name = \"custom3.Custom\",\n"
"    .tp_doc = PyDoc_STR(\"Custom objects\"),\n"
"    .tp_basicsize = sizeof(CustomObject),\n"
"    .tp_itemsize = 0,\n"
"    .tp_flags = Py_TPFLAGS_DEFAULT | Py_TPFLAGS_BASETYPE,\n"
"    .tp_new = Custom_new,\n"
"    .tp_init = Custom_init,\n"
"    .tp_dealloc = Custom_dealloc,\n"
"    .tp_members = Custom_members,\n"
"    .tp_methods = Custom_methods,\n"
"    .tp_getset = Custom_getsetters,\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static int\n"
"custom_module_exec(PyObject *m)\n"
"{\n"
"    if (PyType_Ready(&CustomType) < 0) {\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    if (PyModule_AddObjectRef(m, \"Custom\", (PyObject *) &CustomType) < 0) "
"{\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyModuleDef_Slot custom_module_slots[] = {\n"
"    {Py_mod_exec, custom_module_exec},\n"
"    {Py_mod_multiple_interpreters, "
"Py_MOD_MULTIPLE_INTERPRETERS_NOT_SUPPORTED},\n"
"    {0, NULL}\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static PyModuleDef custom_module = {\n"
"    .m_base = PyModuleDef_HEAD_INIT,\n"
"    .m_name = \"custom3\",\n"
"    .m_doc = \"Example module that creates an extension type.\",\n"
"    .m_size = 0,\n"
"    .m_slots = custom_module_slots,\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"PyMODINIT_FUNC\n"
"PyInit_custom3(void)\n"
"{\n"
"    return PyModuleDef_Init(&custom_module);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"#define PY_SSIZE_T_CLEAN\n"
"#include <Python.h>\n"
"#include <stddef.h> /* für offsetof() */\n"
"\n"
"typedef struct {\n"
"    PyObject_HEAD\n"
"    PyObject *first; /* Vorname */\n"
"    PyObject *last;  /* Nachname */\n"
"    int number;\n"
"} CustomObject;\n"
"\n"
"static void\n"
"Custom_dealloc(PyObject *op)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    Py_XDECREF(self->first);\n"
"    Py_XDECREF(self->last);\n"
"    Py_TYPE(self)->tp_free(self);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyObject *\n"
"Custom_new(PyTypeObject *type, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwds)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self;\n"
"    self = (CustomObject *) type->tp_alloc(type, 0);\n"
"    if (self != NULL) {\n"
"        self->first = Py_GetConstant(Py_CONSTANT_EMPTY_STR);\n"
"        if (self->first == NULL) {\n"
"            Py_DECREF(self);\n"
"            return NULL;\n"
"        }\n"
"        self->last = Py_GetConstant(Py_CONSTANT_EMPTY_STR);\n"
"        if (self->last == NULL) {\n"
"            Py_DECREF(self);\n"
"            return NULL;\n"
"        }\n"
"        self->number = 0;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return (PyObject *) self;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static int\n"
"Custom_init(PyObject *op, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwds)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    static char *kwlist[] = {\"first\", \"last\", \"number\", NULL};\n"
"    PyObject *first = NULL, *last = NULL;\n"
"\n"
"    if (!PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords(args, kwds, \"|UUi\", kwlist,\n"
"                                     &first, &last,\n"
"                                     &self->number))\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"\n"
"    if (first) {\n"
"        Py_SETREF(self->first, Py_NewRef(first));\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (last) {\n"
"        Py_SETREF(self->last, Py_NewRef(last));\n"
"    }\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyMemberDef Custom_members[] = {\n"
"    {\"number\", Py_T_INT, offsetof(CustomObject, number), 0,\n"
"     \"custom number\"},\n"
"    {NULL}  /* Sentinel */\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static PyObject *\n"
"Custom_getfirst(PyObject *op, void *closure)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    return Py_NewRef(self->first);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static int\n"
"Custom_setfirst(PyObject *op, PyObject *value, void *closure)\n"
