#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:711
msgid ""
"First, the traversal method lets the cyclic GC know about subobjects that "
"could participate in cycles::"
msgstr ""
"Erstens informiert die Traversierungsmethode den zyklischen GC über "
"Unterobjekte, die an Zyklen beteiligt sein könnten::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:714
msgid ""
"static int\n"
"Custom_traverse(PyObject *op, visitproc visit, void *arg)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    int vret;\n"
"    if (self->first) {\n"
"        vret = visit(self->first, arg);\n"
"        if (vret != 0)\n"
"            return vret;\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (self->last) {\n"
"        vret = visit(self->last, arg);\n"
"        if (vret != 0)\n"
"            return vret;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"static int\n"
"Custom_traverse(PyObject *op, visitproc visit, void *arg)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    int vret;\n"
"    if (self->first) {\n"
"        vret = visit(self->first, arg);\n"
"        if (vret != 0)\n"
"            return vret;\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (self->last) {\n"
"        vret = visit(self->last, arg);\n"
"        if (vret != 0)\n"
"            return vret;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:732
msgid ""
"For each subobject that can participate in cycles, we need to call the :c:"
"func:`!visit` function, which is passed to the traversal method. The :c:func:"
"`!visit` function takes as arguments the subobject and the extra argument "
"*arg* passed to the traversal method.  It returns an integer value that must "
"be returned if it is non-zero."
msgstr ""
"Für jedes Unterobjekt, das an Zyklen teilnehmen kann, müssen wir die "
"Funktion „ :c:func:`!visit` “ aufrufen, die an die Durchlaufmethode "
"übergeben wird. Die Funktion „ :c:func:`!visit` “ nimmt als Argumente das "
"Unterobjekt und das zusätzliche Argument *arg* entgegen, das an die "
"Durchlaufmethode übergeben wurde. Sie gibt einen ganzzahligen Wert zurück, "
"der zurückgegeben werden muss, sofern er ungleich Null ist."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:738
msgid ""
"Python provides a :c:func:`Py_VISIT` macro that automates calling visit "
"functions.  With :c:func:`Py_VISIT`, we can minimize the amount of "
"boilerplate in ``Custom_traverse``::"
msgstr ""
"Python bietet das Makro „ :c:func:`Py_VISIT` “, das den Aufruf von „visit“-"
"Funktionen automatisiert. Mit „ :c:func:`Py_VISIT` “ können wir den Umfang "
"an Boilerplate-Code in „ ``Custom_traverse`` “ minimieren ::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:742
msgid ""
"static int\n"
"Custom_traverse(PyObject *op, visitproc visit, void *arg)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    Py_VISIT(self->first);\n"
"    Py_VISIT(self->last);\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"static int\n"
"Custom_traverse(PyObject *op, visitproc visit, void *arg)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    Py_VISIT(self->first);\n"
"    Py_VISIT(self->last);\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:752
msgid ""
"The :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_traverse` implementation must name its "
"arguments exactly *visit* and *arg* in order to use :c:func:`Py_VISIT`."
msgstr ""
"Die Implementierung von ` :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_traverse` ` muss ihre "
"Argumente genau *visit* und *arg* nennen, um ` :c:func:`Py_VISIT`` verwenden "
"zu können."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:755
msgid ""
"Second, we need to provide a method for clearing any subobjects that can "
"participate in cycles::"
msgstr ""
"Zweitens müssen wir eine Methode bereitstellen, mit der alle Unterobjekte "
"entfernt werden können, die an Zyklen beteiligt sein könnten::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:758
msgid ""
"static int\n"
"Custom_clear(PyObject *op)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    Py_CLEAR(self->first);\n"
"    Py_CLEAR(self->last);\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"static int\n"
"Custom_clear(PyObject *op)\n"
"{\n"
"    CustomObject *self = (CustomObject *) op;\n"
"    Py_CLEAR(self->first);\n"
"    Py_CLEAR(self->last);\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:767
msgid ""
"Notice the use of the :c:func:`Py_CLEAR` macro.  It is the recommended and "
"safe way to clear data attributes of arbitrary types while decrementing "
"their reference counts.  If you were to call :c:func:`Py_XDECREF` instead on "
"the attribute before setting it to ``NULL``, there is a possibility that the "
"attribute's destructor would call back into code that reads the attribute "
"again (*especially* if there is a reference cycle)."
msgstr ""
"Beachten Sie die Verwendung des Makros „ :c:func:`Py_CLEAR` “. Dies ist die "
"empfohlene und sichere Methode, um Datenattribute beliebiger Typen zu "
"löschen und gleichzeitig deren Referenzzähler zu verringern.  Wenn Sie "
"stattdessen vor dem Setzen des Attributs auf ` ``NULL``` die Funktion ` :c:"
"func:`Py_XDECREF` ` aufrufen würden, besteht die Möglichkeit, dass der "
"Destruktor des Attributs erneut Code aufruft, der das Attribut erneut "
"ausliest (*insbesondere*, wenn ein Referenzzyklus vorliegt)."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:775
msgid "You could emulate :c:func:`Py_CLEAR` by writing::"
msgstr ""
"Du könntest „ :c:func:`Py_CLEAR` “ nachahmen, indem du Folgendes schreibst::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:777
msgid ""
"PyObject *tmp;\n"
"tmp = self->first;\n"
"self->first = NULL;\n"
"Py_XDECREF(tmp);"
msgstr ""
"PyObject *tmp;\n"
"tmp = self->first;\n"
"self->first = NULL;\n"
"Py_XDECREF(tmp);"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:782
msgid ""
"Nevertheless, it is much easier and less error-prone to always use :c:func:"
"`Py_CLEAR` when deleting an attribute.  Don't try to micro-optimize at the "
"expense of robustness!"
msgstr ""
"Dennoch ist es viel einfacher und weniger fehleranfällig, beim Löschen eines "
"Attributs stets ` :c:func:`Py_CLEAR` ` zu verwenden. Versuchen Sie nicht, "
"auf Kosten der Robustheit Mikrooptimierungen vorzunehmen!"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:786
msgid ""
"The deallocator ``Custom_dealloc`` may call arbitrary code when clearing "
"attributes.  It means the circular GC can be triggered inside the function. "
"Since the GC assumes reference count is not zero, we need to untrack the "
"object from the GC by calling :c:func:`PyObject_GC_UnTrack` before clearing "
"members. Here is our reimplemented deallocator using :c:func:"
"`PyObject_GC_UnTrack` and ``Custom_clear``::"
msgstr ""
"Der Deallocator ``Custom_dealloc`` ruft beim Löschen von Attributen "
"möglicherweise beliebigen Code auf. Das bedeutet, dass innerhalb der "
"Funktion ein zirkulärer GC ausgelöst werden kann. Da der GC davon ausgeht, "
"dass die Referenzanzahl ungleich Null ist, müssen wir das Objekt aus dem GC "
"entfernen, indem wir vor dem Löschen der Mitglieder :c:func:"
"`PyObject_GC_UnTrack` aufrufen. Hier ist unser neu implementierter "
"Deallocator unter Verwendung von :c:func:`PyObject_GC_UnTrack` und "
"``Custom_clear``::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:793
msgid ""
"static void\n"
"Custom_dealloc(PyObject *op)\n"
"{\n"
"    PyObject_GC_UnTrack(op);\n"
"    (void)Custom_clear(op);\n"
"    Py_TYPE(op)->tp_free(op);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"static void\n"
"Custom_dealloc(PyObject *op)\n"
"{\n"
"    PyObject_GC_UnTrack(op);\n"
"    (void)Custom_clear(op);\n"
"    Py_TYPE(op)->tp_free(op);\n"
"}"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:801
msgid ""
"Finally, we add the :c:macro:`Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_GC` flag to the class flags::"
msgstr ""
"Abschließend fügen wir das Flag „ :c:macro:`Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_GC` “ zu den "
"Klassenflags hinzu::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:803
msgid ""
".tp_flags = Py_TPFLAGS_DEFAULT | Py_TPFLAGS_BASETYPE | Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_GC,"
msgstr ""
".tp_flags = Py_TPFLAGS_DEFAULT | Py_TPFLAGS_BASETYPE | Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_GC,"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:805
msgid ""
"That's pretty much it.  If we had written custom :c:member:`~PyTypeObject."
"tp_alloc` or :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_free` handlers, we'd need to modify "
"them for cyclic garbage collection.  Most extensions will use the versions "
"automatically provided."
msgstr ""
"Das war’s im Grunde schon. Hätten wir eigene Handler für „ :c:member:"
"`~PyTypeObject.tp_alloc` “ oder „ :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_free` “ "
"geschrieben, müssten wir diese für die zyklische Garbage Collection "
"anpassen. Die meisten Erweiterungen verwenden die automatisch "
"bereitgestellten Versionen."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:811
msgid "Subclassing other types"
msgstr "Unterklassen anderer Typen"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:813
msgid ""
"It is possible to create new extension types that are derived from existing "
"types. It is easiest to inherit from the built in types, since an extension "
"can easily use the :c:type:`PyTypeObject` it needs. It can be difficult to "
"share these :c:type:`PyTypeObject` structures between extension modules."
msgstr ""
"Es ist möglich, neue Erweiterungsarten zu erstellen, die von bestehenden "
"Arten abgeleitet sind. Am einfachsten ist es, von den integrierten Arten zu "
"erben, da eine Erweiterung die benötigten „ :c:type:`PyTypeObject` “ "
"problemlos nutzen kann. Es kann schwierig sein, diese „ :c:type:"
"`PyTypeObject` “-Strukturen zwischen Erweiterungsmodulen gemeinsam zu nutzen."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:818
msgid ""
"In this example we will create a :class:`!SubList` type that inherits from "
"the built-in :class:`list` type. The new type will be completely compatible "
"with regular lists, but will have an additional :meth:`!increment` method "
"that increases an internal counter:"
msgstr ""
"In diesem Beispiel erstellen wir einen Typ „ :class:`!SubList` “, der vom "
"integrierten Typ „ :class:`list` “ abgeleitet ist. Der neue Typ ist "
"vollständig kompatibel mit regulären Listen, verfügt jedoch über eine "
"zusätzliche Methode „ :meth:`!increment` “, die einen internen Zähler erhöht:"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:823
msgid ""
">>> import sublist\n"
">>> s = sublist.SubList(range(3))\n"
">>> s.extend(s)\n"
">>> print(len(s))\n"
"6\n"
">>> print(s.increment())\n"
"1\n"
">>> print(s.increment())\n"
"2"
msgstr ""
">>> import sublist\n"
">>> s = sublist.SubList(range(3))\n"
">>> s.extend(s)\n"
">>> print(len(s))\n"
"6\n"
">>> print(s.increment())\n"
"1\n"
">>> print(s.increment())\n"
"2"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:835
msgid ""
"#define PY_SSIZE_T_CLEAN\n"
"#include <Python.h>\n"
"\n"
"typedef struct {\n"
"    PyListObject list;\n"
"    int state;\n"
"} SubListObject;\n"
"\n"
"static PyObject *\n"
"SubList_increment(PyObject *op, PyObject *Py_UNUSED(dummy))\n"
"{\n"
"    SubListObject *self = (SubListObject *) op;\n"
"    self->state++;\n"
"    return PyLong_FromLong(self->state);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyMethodDef SubList_methods[] = {\n"
"    {\"increment\", SubList_increment, METH_NOARGS,\n"
"     PyDoc_STR(\"increment state counter\")},\n"
"    {NULL},\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static int\n"
"SubList_init(PyObject *op, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwds)\n"
"{\n"
"    SubListObject *self = (SubListObject *) op;\n"
"    if (PyList_Type.tp_init(op, args, kwds) < 0)\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    self->state = 0;\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyTypeObject SubListType = {\n"
"    .ob_base = PyVarObject_HEAD_INIT(NULL, 0)\n"
"    .tp_name = \"sublist.SubList\",\n"
"    .tp_doc = PyDoc_STR(\"SubList objects\"),\n"
"    .tp_basicsize = sizeof(SubListObject),\n"
"    .tp_itemsize = 0,\n"
"    .tp_flags = Py_TPFLAGS_DEFAULT | Py_TPFLAGS_BASETYPE,\n"
"    .tp_init = SubList_init,\n"
"    .tp_methods = SubList_methods,\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static int\n"
"sublist_module_exec(PyObject *m)\n"
"{\n"
"    SubListType.tp_base = &PyList_Type;\n"
"    if (PyType_Ready(&SubListType) < 0) {\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    if (PyModule_AddObjectRef(m, \"SubList\", (PyObject *) &SubListType) < "
"0) {\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyModuleDef_Slot sublist_module_slots[] = {\n"
"    {Py_mod_exec, sublist_module_exec},\n"
"    {Py_mod_multiple_interpreters, "
"Py_MOD_MULTIPLE_INTERPRETERS_NOT_SUPPORTED},\n"
"    {0, NULL}\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static PyModuleDef sublist_module = {\n"
"    .m_base = PyModuleDef_HEAD_INIT,\n"
"    .m_name = \"sublist\",\n"
"    .m_doc = \"Example module that creates an extension type.\",\n"
"    .m_size = 0,\n"
"    .m_slots = sublist_module_slots,\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"PyMODINIT_FUNC\n"
"PyInit_sublist(void)\n"
"{\n"
"    return PyModuleDef_Init(&sublist_module);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"#define PY_SSIZE_T_CLEAN\n"
"#include <Python.h>\n"
"\n"
"typedef struct {\n"
"    PyListObject list;\n"
"    int state;\n"
"} SubListObject;\n"
"\n"
"static PyObject *\n"
"SubList_increment(PyObject *op, PyObject *Py_UNUSED(dummy))\n"
"{\n"
"    SubListObject *self = (SubListObject *) op;\n"
"    self->state++;\n"
"    return PyLong_FromLong(self->state);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyMethodDef SubList_methods[] = {\n"
"    {\"increment\", SubList_increment, METH_NOARGS,\n"
"     PyDoc_STR(\"Zähler für den Zustand erhöhen\")},\n"
"    {NULL},\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static int\n"
"SubList_init(PyObject *op, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwds)\n"
"{\n"
"    SubListObject *self = (SubListObject *) op;\n"
"    if (PyList_Type.tp_init(op, args, kwds) < 0)\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    self->state = 0;\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyTypeObject SubListType = {\n"
"    .ob_base = PyVarObject_HEAD_INIT(NULL, 0)\n"
"    .tp_name = „sublist.SubList“,\n"
"    .tp_doc = PyDoc_STR(„SubList-Objekte“),\n"
"    .tp_basicsize = sizeof(SubListObject),\n"
"    .tp_itemsize = 0,\n"
"    .tp_flags = Py_TPFLAGS_DEFAULT | Py_TPFLAGS_BASETYPE,\n"
"    .tp_init = SubList_init,\n"
"    .tp_methods = SubList_methods,\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static int\n"
"sublist_module_exec(PyObject *m)\n"
"{\n"
"    SubListType.tp_base = &PyList_Type;\n"
"    if (PyType_Ready(&SubListType) < 0) {\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    if (PyModule_AddObjectRef(m, „SubList“, (PyObject *) &SubListType) < 0) "
"{\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"static PyModuleDef_Slot sublist_module_slots[] = {\n"
"    {Py_mod_exec, sublist_module_exec},\n"
"    {Py_mod_multiple_interpreters, "
"Py_MOD_MULTIPLE_INTERPRETERS_NOT_SUPPORTED},\n"
"    {0, NULL}\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"static PyModuleDef sublist_module = {\n"
"    .m_base = PyModuleDef_HEAD_INIT,\n"
"    .m_name = \"sublist\",\n"
"    .m_doc = \"Beispielmodul, das einen Erweiterungstyp erstellt.\",\n"
"    .m_size = 0,\n"
"    .m_slots = sublist_module_slots,\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"PyMODINIT_FUNC\n"
"PyInit_sublist(void)\n"
"{\n"
"    return PyModuleDef_Init(&sublist_module);\n"
"}\n"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:838
msgid ""
"As you can see, the source code closely resembles the :class:`!Custom` "
"examples in previous sections. We will break down the main differences "
"between them. ::"
msgstr ""
"Wie Sie sehen können, ähnelt der Quellcode stark den Beispielen unter „ :"
"class:`!Custom` “ aus den vorangegangenen Abschnitten. Wir werden die "
"wichtigsten Unterschiede zwischen ihnen näher erläutern. ::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:841
msgid ""
"typedef struct {\n"
"    PyListObject list;\n"
"    int state;\n"
"} SubListObject;"
msgstr ""
"typedef struct {\n"
"    PyListObject list;\n"
"    int state;\n"
"} SubListObject;"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:846
msgid ""
"The primary difference for derived type objects is that the base type's "
"object structure must be the first value.  The base type will already "
"include the :c:func:`PyObject_HEAD` at the beginning of its structure."
msgstr ""
"Der wesentliche Unterschied bei Objekten abgeleiteter Typen besteht darin, "
"dass die Objektstruktur des Basistyps als erster Wert stehen muss. Der "
"Basistyp enthält bereits die „ :c:func:`PyObject_HEAD` “ am Anfang seiner "
"Struktur."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:850
msgid ""
"When a Python object is a :class:`!SubList` instance, its ``PyObject *`` "
"pointer can be safely cast to both ``PyListObject *`` and ``SubListObject "
"*``::"
msgstr ""
"Wenn ein Python-Objekt eine Instanz von ` :class:`!SubList` ` ist, kann sein "
"` ``PyObject *`` `-Zeiger problemlos sowohl in ` ``PyListObject *`` ` als "
"auch in ` ``SubListObject *``` umgewandelt werden ::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:853
msgid ""
"static int\n"
"SubList_init(PyObject *op, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwds)\n"
"{\n"
"    SubListObject *self = (SubListObject *) op;\n"
"    if (PyList_Type.tp_init(op, args, kwds) < 0)\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    self->state = 0;\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"static int\n"
"SubList_init(PyObject *op, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwds)\n"
"{\n"
"    SubListObject *self = (SubListObject *) op;\n"
"    if (PyList_Type.tp_init(op, args, kwds) < 0)\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    self->state = 0;\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:863
msgid ""
"We see above how to call through to the :meth:`~object.__init__` method of "
"the base type."
msgstr ""
"Oben sehen wir, wie man die Methode „ :meth:`~object.__init__` “ des "
"Basistyps aufruft."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:866
msgid ""
"This pattern is important when writing a type with custom :c:member:"
"`~PyTypeObject.tp_new` and :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_dealloc` members.  "
"The :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new` handler should not actually create the "
"memory for the object with its :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_alloc`, but let "
"the base class handle it by calling its own :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new`."
msgstr ""
"Dieses Muster ist wichtig, wenn man einen Typ mit benutzerdefinierten ` :c:"
"member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new` `- und ` :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_dealloc` "
"`-Mitgliedern definiert. Der ` :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new` `-Handler "
"sollte den Speicher für das Objekt nicht selbst mit ` :c:member:"
"`~PyTypeObject.tp_alloc`` anlegen, sondern dies der Basisklasse überlassen, "
"indem er deren ` :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_new`` aufruft."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:872
msgid ""
"The :c:type:`PyTypeObject` struct supports a :c:member:`~PyTypeObject."
"tp_base` specifying the type's concrete base class.  Due to cross-platform "
"compiler issues, you can't fill that field directly with a reference to :c:"
"type:`PyList_Type`; it should be done in the :c:data:`Py_mod_exec` function::"
msgstr ""
"Die Struktur „ :c:type:`PyTypeObject` “ unterstützt ein Feld „ :c:member:"
"`~PyTypeObject.tp_base` “, das die konkrete Basisklasse des Typs angibt. "
"Aufgrund plattformübergreifender Compiler-Probleme kannst du dieses Feld "
"nicht direkt mit einem Verweis auf „ :c:type:`PyList_Type` “ füllen; dies "
"sollte in der Funktion „ :c:data:`Py_mod_exec` “ erfolgen::"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:878
msgid ""
"static int\n"
"sublist_module_exec(PyObject *m)\n"
"{\n"
"    SubListType.tp_base = &PyList_Type;\n"
"    if (PyType_Ready(&SubListType) < 0) {\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    if (PyModule_AddObjectRef(m, \"SubList\", (PyObject *) &SubListType) < "
"0) {\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"static int\n"
"sublist_module_exec(PyObject *m)\n"
"{\n"
"    SubListType.tp_base = &PyList_Type;\n"
"    if (PyType_Ready(&SubListType) < 0) {\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    if (PyModule_AddObjectRef(m, „SubList“, (PyObject *) &SubListType) < 0) "
"{\n"
"        return -1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:893
msgid ""
"Before calling :c:func:`PyType_Ready`, the type structure must have the :c:"
"member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_base` slot filled in.  When we are deriving an "
"existing type, it is not necessary to fill out the :c:member:`~PyTypeObject."
"tp_alloc` slot with :c:func:`PyType_GenericNew` -- the allocation function "
"from the base type will be inherited."
msgstr ""
"Bevor „ :c:func:`PyType_Ready` “ aufgerufen wird, muss im Feld „ :c:member:"
"`~PyTypeObject.tp_base` “ der Typstruktur ein Wert eingetragen sein. Wenn "
"wir einen bestehenden Typ ableiten, ist es nicht erforderlich, das Feld „ :c:"
"member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_alloc` “ mit „ :c:func:`PyType_GenericNew` “ zu "
"füllen – die Zuweisungsfunktion des Basistyps wird übernommen."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:899
msgid ""
"After that, calling :c:func:`PyType_Ready` and adding the type object to the "
"module is the same as with the basic :class:`!Custom` examples."
msgstr ""
"Danach entspricht der Aufruf von „ :c:func:`PyType_Ready` “ und das "
"Hinzufügen des Typobjekts zum Modul dem Vorgehen in den grundlegenden „ :"
"class:`!Custom` “-Beispielen."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:904
msgid "Footnotes"
msgstr "Fußnoten"

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:905
msgid ""
"This is true when we know that the object is a basic type, like a string or "
"a float."
msgstr ""
"Das trifft zu, wenn wir wissen, dass es sich bei dem Objekt um einen "
"Grundtyp handelt, wie beispielsweise eine Zeichenkette oder eine "
"Gleitkommazahl."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:908
msgid ""
"We relied on this in the :c:member:`~PyTypeObject.tp_dealloc` handler in "
"this example, because our type doesn't support garbage collection."
msgstr ""
"In diesem Beispiel haben wir im Handler „ :c:member:`~PyTypeObject."
"tp_dealloc` “ darauf zurückgegriffen, da unser Typ keine Garbage Collection "
"unterstützt."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:911
msgid ""
"We now know that the first and last members are strings, so perhaps we could "
"be less careful about decrementing their reference counts, however, we "
"accept instances of string subclasses.  Even though deallocating normal "
"strings won't call back into our objects, we can't guarantee that "
"deallocating an instance of a string subclass won't call back into our "
"objects."
msgstr ""
"Wir wissen nun, dass das erste und das letzte Element Zeichenketten sind, "
"daher könnten wir beim Verringern ihrer Referenzzähler vielleicht etwas "
"weniger vorsichtig vorgehen; allerdings akzeptieren wir auch Instanzen von "
"Unterklassen von Zeichenketten.  Auch wenn die Freigabe normaler "
"Zeichenketten keinen Rückruf in unsere Objekte auslöst, können wir nicht "
"garantieren, dass die Freigabe einer Instanz einer Zeichenketten-Unterklasse "
"keinen Rückruf in unsere Objekte auslöst."

#: ../../extending/newtypes_tutorial.rst:917
msgid ""
"Also, even with our attributes restricted to strings instances, the user "
"could pass arbitrary :class:`str` subclasses and therefore still create "
"reference cycles."
msgstr ""
"Außerdem könnte der Benutzer, selbst wenn unsere Attribute auf Instanzen von "
"„strings“ beschränkt wären, beliebige Unterklassen von „ :class:`str` “ "
"übergeben und somit weiterhin Referenzzyklen erzeugen."
